#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:2
msgid "The kernel snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:4
msgid ""
"The kernel snap is responsible for providing the Linux kernel image and "
"modules for the system. The kernel snap to be used is defined in the "
"device's model assertion, which is produced and signed by the Brand "
"authority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:8
msgid ""
"Canonical publishes some reference kernel snaps as well as kernel snaps for "
"main Canonical models such as official Ubuntu Core VMs on various certified "
"public clouds, as well as general purpose computing images for popular "
"physical devices such as the 64-bit x86 PC and Raspberry Pi."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:13
msgid ""
"For details on building a kernel snap, see [Build a kernel snap](https://"
"documentation.ubuntu.com/core/how-to-guides/image-creation/build-a-kernel-"
"snap/) in the Ubuntu Core documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:16
msgid "Setup files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:18
msgid ""
"In addition to traditional snap metadata, the kernel snap also holds some "
"setup files fundamental to the initialization and lifecycle of the device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:21
msgid "The layout for a kernel snap has some variation, but usually follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:23
msgid ""
"`meta/snap.yaml` - Traditional snap details, with `type: kernel` explicitly "
"defined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:24
msgid ""
"`meta/kernel.yaml` - Optional kernel-specific metadata defining kernel-"
"provided assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:25
msgid "`snapd-info` - Information about the snapd packaged in the initrd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:26
msgid ""
"`modules/<version>/` - Kernel modules; version must match the one in "
"`snap.yaml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:27
msgid "`firmware/` - Optional firmware files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:28
msgid ""
"`dtbs/` - Optional binary device-tree files, if gadget.yaml states `device-"
"tree-origin: kernel`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:29
msgid "kernel - The actual kernel image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:30
msgid "initrd - The initrd image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:32
msgid ""
"The kernel and initrd may be discrete objects, usually named `kernel.img` "
"and `initrd.img`, respectively. However, they could also be distributed as a "
"single [Unified Kernel Image](https://uapi-group.org/specifications/specs/"
"unified_kernel_image/) (UKI) or as a [Flatted Image Tree](https://"
"fitspec.osfw.foundation/) (FIT) image. These are usually named `kernel.efi` "
"or `kernel.img`, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:37
msgid "kernel.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:39
msgid ""
"The `kernel.yaml` provides information used by snapd to determine kernel-"
"specific asset information. Primarily, this is about device trees and kernel "
"modules. The standard format is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:43
msgid ""
"dynamic-modules: $SNAP_DATA\n"
"assets:\n"
"  dtbs:\n"
"    update: true\n"
"    content:\n"
"      - dtbs/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:52
msgid ""
"`dynamic-modules` points to a folder which contains `modules/` and `firmware/"
"` directories, usually created by a kernel component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:55
msgid ""
"`assets` details a list of content the kernel snap provides, usually device "
"tree files, to the gadget snap. These are then citable in the gadget snap's "
"`gadget.yaml` like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:59
msgid ""
"volumes:\n"
"  platform:\n"
"    schema: gpt\n"
"    bootloader: grub\n"
"    structure:\n"
"      - name: ubuntu-seed\n"
"        role: system-seed\n"
"        filesystem: vfat\n"
"        type: C12A7328-F81F-11D2-BA4B-00A0C93EC93B\n"
"        size: 800M\n"
"        offset: 8M\n"
"        content:\n"
"          - source: $kernel:dtbs/dtbs/\n"
"            target: /dtbs/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/development/yaml-schemas/the-kernel-snap.md:76
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"TODO -- document the initrd more thoroughly\n"
"## initrd\n"
"\n"
"The initrd component of the kernel snap plays a fundamental role in the "
"booting\n"
"of an Ubuntu Core system.\n"
"\n"
"The initrd is usually built using the ubuntu-core-initramfs tool.\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""
